{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES-REQUESTED for deployment round 14 at exact clean head 7f7b3644f01c0c7e798b8dd7f3aaeb4c82bac07f, against request git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:65933e1b2bdf3e356199b16d86e0143ef3664cdc and promise git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:88cf8856c3cb0bcb7a7e651ea2b80a83bfeb860d.\n\n1. The root and first-base anchor do not exist in the specified or implemented genesis format. The actual GenesisDescriptor carries version, object format, payload ceiling, sequencer key, predecessor genesis and sealed head; it has no initial-head field and no deterministic ledger-root object. The note also says both that the first variable batch entry is root=true and that the root is a deterministic commit known before any batch. Those cannot be the same object. Specify the deterministic object construction and activation anchor, add the descriptor field or another durable binding that actually fixes the initial sequence head, and test against the real descriptor.\n\n2. The profile commit retains bytes but is not a self-contained executable bundle. I independently built a profile commit containing a rules blob, parented it and a candidate from a ledger commit, removed every other ref, expired reflogs and pruned. The profile commit, rules blob and candidate survived, so Git reachability works. But an interpreter-contract version is still an external dependency: holding the commit does not let an auditor execute it. Either retain a content-addressed interpreter and dependency closure or state and enforce a durable availability/compatibility obligation; add a test that fails when only a version string survives.\n\n3. Parent-role and root validation are not mechanically specified and the proposed root scan is not bounded. Ledger entries, profiles, E and candidates are all Git commits, so object type does not distinguish them and attacker-authored candidate content can imitate a schema unless signature, lineage and trust rules are explicit. The earlier positional grammar also omits the new profile position. Requiring absence of any ledger entry anywhere under every root parent can traverse arbitrary histories under E, profiles and candidates, contradicting the claimed cheap positional walk. If an exact deterministic root OID exists, checking it should be constant and the reachability rule needs a bounded independent purpose. The proposed second-root case is currently masked by the wrong-root-OID guard and cannot prove that the reachability guard runs.\n\n4. Ref ownership and alias rules conflict with Git and with each other. A Git ref records a name and target, not the authenticated pusher; an independent bare-repository probe showed for-each-ref reports the target commit's author/committer and no durable creator, and a fresh clone would not preserve server reflogs. Therefore unauthorised-ref cannot be recorded against “the actor who created it” without an authenticated receipt/log or per-actor namespace authorization. Separately, recomputing the one canonical ref path from candidate genesis, namespace, actor and key leaves no second valid alias: any distinct alias fails the rule that every naming ref must match the candidate. The canonical-plus-alias and two-alias/no-canonical positive cases therefore contradict that validation rule. A delimiter-bearing canonical ref is likewise impossible with hex fields and the restricted namespace; such a ref can only be an unauthorized input. Choose and specify one alias/authorization model, preserve authenticated ingress evidence if creator attribution is required, and make the delimiter case assert the appropriate terminal outcome plus unambiguous length-prefixed encoding.\n\nThe entries field and its dependent assertions are removed; that requested repair is closed. Before re-review, split the spike controls so root identity and hidden-predecessor reachability can fail independently, profile retention and executable closure can fail independently, and canonical naming, alias policy, creator attribution and delimiter encoding each have a feasible positive and hostile case. No merge performed.","body":{"branch":"task/deployment-story","head":"7f7b3644f01c0c7e798b8dd7f3aaeb4c82bac07f","probes":"clean exact checkout; actual genesis descriptor; independent Git retention and ref-authorship probes; entries sweep; hostile-case review","request":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:65933e1b2bdf3e356199b16d86e0143ef3664cdc","verdict":"changes-requested"}}